messages[12]{user,text}:
  user_1,[00:00] Hello? Umm... is this Suresh from Secure Life Solutions?
  user_2,[00:05] Yes, hi Dev, this is Suresh. I can hear you, can you hear me?
  user_1,[00:10] Yeah, yeah... I can hear you. Thanks. I was calling about my health policy.
  user_2,[00:15] Sure, let me pull up your details. One sec... [typing]
  user_2,[00:25] ...Okay, I see here your policy number is HL-45789 and it's... uh... expired as of 15/08/2026.
  user_1,[00:30] Oh no, expired? I thought it was still active.
  user_2,[00:35] Yeah, the system shows it lapsed. Did you get a renewal notice?
  user_1,[00:40] I... I don’t think so. I guess I missed it.
  user_2,[00:45] No worries, we can discuss renewal options. Or if you want to let it stay expired, that's fine too.
  user_1,[00:50] Honestly, I’m not sure I need it anymore. I’ve been... [sighs] ...considering switching.
  user_2,[00:55] I understand. If you decide to let it stay expired, we’ll close it in the system. If you want a new policy, I can quote you right now.
  user_1,[01:00] Let’s... let’s keep it expired for now. I’ll think about it later. Thanks for confirming.